# Frontend configuration.
#
# Copy to `frontend/.env.local`. Every NEXT_PUBLIC_* value is inlined at build time, so a
# deployment must supply them to the *build*, not only to the running container.

# --- chain ---
NEXT_PUBLIC_MONAD_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8545

# Which Monad. 143 is mainnet, 10143 is testnet. NOT defaulted: the two are indistinguishable from
# inside the app — one built for either and pointed at the other renders perfectly, and the only
# symptom is that every address resolves to nothing.
#
# Note that DOKU can only run on 143 today. Uniswap v4 is not deployed on Monad testnet, so a
# market there can launch and fill and then has nowhere to graduate into.
NEXT_PUBLIC_MONAD_CHAIN_ID=143

# --- DOKU's own contracts ---
#
# The app refuses to start without them rather than defaulting to the zero address, which is a
# real address that accepts MON and never gives it back.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOKU_FACTORY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOKU_GRADUATION=
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOKU_REGISTRY=
# The hook. Needed for a reason the others are not: it is a field of every `PoolKey`, so a swap on
# a graduated market cannot even be ADDRESSED without it.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOKU_HOOK=

# --- Uniswap v4, which DOKU integrates with rather than deploys ---
#
# Mainnet (143) values below. All five are required: without them a graduated market cannot be
# traded at all, and a market that graduates is the successful case.
NEXT_PUBLIC_V4_POOL_MANAGER=0x188d586Ddcf52439676Ca21A244753fA19F9Ea8e
NEXT_PUBLIC_V4_POSITION_MANAGER=0x5b7eC4a94fF9beDb700fb82aB09d5846972F4016
NEXT_PUBLIC_V4_QUOTER=0xa222dd357a9076d1091ed6aa2e16c9742dd26891
NEXT_PUBLIC_V4_STATE_VIEW=0x77395f3b2e73Ae90843717371294FA97cc419D64
NEXT_PUBLIC_PERMIT2=0x000000000022D473030F116dDEE9F6B43aC78BA3

# UniversalRouter, and WHICH one is a measurement rather than a lookup. Two are live on Monad
# mainnet; sampling 400 blocks of real v4 `Swap` logs and tallying the caller gave 14 of 55 swaps
# to this one and ZERO to the newer v2.1.1 (0xFdf682F51FE81Aa4898F0AE2163d8A55c127fbC7).
# Re-measure before launch — this is a deployment fact and it can move.
NEXT_PUBLIC_UNIVERSAL_ROUTER=0x0d97dc33264bfc1c226207428a79b26757fb9dc3

# --- the zap router (periphery, OPTIONAL) ---
#
# Buying a market with native MON when it is priced in something else, and selling one back into
# MON. Unset, the whole feature is GONE rather than broken: no "pay with MON" control renders on a
# curve market, and nothing else in the app changes. That is deliberate — `sideAssetOptions` in
# `lib/chain/zap-plan.ts` is the single gate, and a disabled control on a feature with no contract
# behind it is a promise somebody has to break.
#
# It was missing from this file entirely until 2026-09-10, which meant anyone setting up from the
# example got a build with the feature silently absent and nothing telling them why.
#
# A GRADUATED market still offers MON with this unset — that path is one Uniswap multi-hop and
# needs no router of ours.
#
# Mainnet, generation 3 v2 (buys AND sells). v1 `0x8e1630b8…` buys only; the gen-2 router
# `0x4B5aEC46…` is bound to a paused factory and reverts `UnknownMarket` on every current market.
# See docs/doku/deployments.md.
NEXT_PUBLIC_ZAP_ROUTER=0x642A984cd29459451Fd5922c3CD92f498e69cb50

# NEXT_PUBLIC_WMON_ADDRESS is GONE. A v4 pool holds native MON directly, so there is no wrapper to
# name — and with it went the swap-then-unwrap a V3 sell needed.

# --- indexer ---
# Server-side, so it may be a private address.
DOKU_INDEXER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3010

# The live feed, as a browser can reach it. Unset means polling only — slower, still correct.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DOKU_LIVE_URL=ws://127.0.0.1:3010/live

# --- optional ---
# With no price source there is no USD anywhere in the app and no currency toggle. A quote older
# than ten minutes is treated as absent: a stale price still renders and still looks live.
# MON_USD_PRICE_URL=https://api.coingecko.com/api/v3/simple/price?ids=monad&vs_currencies=usd
# MON_USD_PRICE_PATH=monad.usd

# Gates launching behind the merkle allowlist. Off unless explicitly enabled.
NEXT_PUBLIC_IS_ALLOWLIST_ENABLED=false

# Third-party liquidity provision (`/pools`). Off unless set; `middleware.ts` answers 404 while it
# is, and every link to the route is hidden.
#
# Both original objections are gone. The page called Uniswap V3's `NonfungiblePositionManager`,
# none of whose functions exist in v4, so every button reverted — it is built on
# `modifyLiquidities` with encoded actions now. And the canonical pool's LP fee is still ZERO by
# construction — the levy is skimmed from the swap's own flash accounting, which a non-zero fee
# makes impossible — but `DokuHook.LP_LEVY_BPS` donates seventy-five basis points of every swap's
# levy to the pool's in-range positions, so a provider earns from volume without the pool charging.
#
# Two reasons it is still a flag. Markets graduated under an earlier hook keep that hook and their
# providers still earn nothing. And the panel's arithmetic is MON-only — it scales both sides by
# eighteen decimals — so it refuses a market quoted in anything else rather than showing figures
# that are off by a factor of 1e12. See `lib/feature-flags.ts`.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LIQUIDITY_ENABLED=false

# Any string of 8+ characters. Used to hash addresses in the verification cookie.
HASH_SEED=doku-local-development-seed

# --- image uploads ---
#
# `/api/uploads/image` re-encodes what a launcher picks, pins it, and registers the CID with the
# indexer so the reference survives a garbage collection. Without a JWT the route answers 503 and
# the launch form says images are unavailable — which is a working launchpad without logos, not a
# broken one.
# PINATA_JWT=
# The bearer the upload route presents to the indexer when registering a pinned CID. Must match the
# indexer's own `UPLOADS_TOKEN`.
# UPLOADS_TOKEN=

# --- preview and development ---
#
# Two different things, and both are opt-in.
#
# `DOKU_CARD_PREVIEW` lets `/explore` and a market page fall back to a fabricated fixture when the
# indexer returned NOTHING, so the cards, the grid and the hero can be reviewed with no service
# running. One real market switches it off; fabricated rows never appear beside real ones.
# DOKU_CARD_PREVIEW=true
#
# `NEXT_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_MODE` says the INDEXER is serving generated markets (set alongside its
# `DOKU_SEED`). It only makes the interface label them, which is the point: a seeded deployment is
# indistinguishable from a real one by design.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_PREVIEW_MODE=false

# Where the merkle allowlist lives. Defaults to `data/allowlist.json` under the working directory.
# DOKU_ALLOWLIST_PATH=

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CDN_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_LINKS={"x":"","github":"","discord":"","tos":""}
# GEOBLOCKED={"countries":[],"regions":[]}
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ARENA_ENABLED=false
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CULT_ENABLED=false
